    {
      "op": "note",
      "text": "Branch of yesman.actions.json: its steps are copied up to the Fort's Securitron vault under Yes Man's line (VMQYesMan01a, the bunker's triggers walked). Instead of waking the army at the console, the player shoots the vault's three power regulators (two DamageObject hits each, as in legion.actions.json). SecuritronVaultExplodeQuestScript blows the vault and, with VMQYesMan01a's objective 48 shown, sets its stage 110 (the army destroyed)."
    },
    {
      "op": "note",
      "text": "Path: Benny killed in his suite with the Platinum Chip taken (VMQTops 80). Yes Man is met at the Tops (first greeting, intro, chip, Benny, Topic003, Topic008, Topic009: the plan, which starts VMQYesMan01 with objective 50 and VMQYesMan02). House is removed through the Lucky 38 control-room terminal (unseal, then disable the cerebral interface). Yes Man (Topic049) moves to the Lucky 38, takes the chip, uploads himself (70), sends the player to the basement (75) and narrates the Securitron upgrade (80, 100). The five tribes' outcomes are given, each walked in its own chain: Boomers pledged (volare.actions.json, VStoryEventBoomers 1), Khans with the NCR (khans.actions.json, VStoryEventKhans 1), Omertas' plot foiled (how-little-we-know.actions.json, VStoryEventRacket 1), Brotherhood allied with the NCR (brotherhood.actions.json, VStoryEventBoS 1), White Glove Society's Ted brought home (beyond-the-beef.actions.json, VMS18 objective 80; objective 79, exposing Mortimer at his banquet, is the other way Yes Man accepts and is not walked); they are reported one by one (VMQYesMan02 100). The Fort bunker's army is activated (VMQYesMan01a 100); the override chip goes into El Dorado (VMQYesMan03 objective 90); Yes Man's Topic056 / Topic067 sets VMQYesMan03 100. The dam battle continues in dam-panel.actions.json."
    },
